# Adjustable Background Translucency

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2-M4 Requested rendering change
Dependencies: 05_WINDOW_SHELL.todo, 06_CAPTURE_POLICY.todo

## Purpose

Let the owner see/read actual content behind the notes while keeping note/transcript text solid.

## Tasks

- [x] Probe a layered WPF window with native chrome and capture affinity before changing the UI.
- [x] Add a background-only opacity slider,10-100% with55% default; do not fade the text/window.
- [x] Remove opaque editor/transcript fills; retain opaque header/setup/confirmation controls.
- [x] Keep the slider enabled in Present and preserve HWND, notes, and removed-acknowledgment behavior.
- [x] Exercise alpha endpoints, solid text, caption/resize/editor hit regions and local capture samples.
- [ ] Complete the affected actual meeting/OBS capture matrix on supported hardware.
- [ ] Record owner readability/usability acceptance with their presentation backgrounds.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] 10% produces real background alpha26,100% produces255, while text/Window opacity stays1.
- [x] Caption returns HTCAPTION, resize edge HTLEFT, editor HTCLIENT in native hit testing.
- [x] No permission/rehearsal prompt or microphone/cloud capture path is introduced.
- [ ] Exact packaged current-rendering configuration is covered by required product qualification.
- [ ] Owner can comfortably read relevant content behind the note surface.

